    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22ykMMYap3WBMUhHviqhAoA)_\n\nStacked on #20 (which is stacked on #19, #18 and #17). Merge in order and GitHub retargets each one.\n\n**Before:** about thirty modules spelled out `~/notes`, `~/bibliography`, `~/Documents/literature`, `~/src` and the like, so the configuration only worked with one machine's layout and a test run could not be kept away from the real notes. `init.el` ended in a Custom block with a list of `/Users/siainbuletin/notes/...` agenda files, which made `org-agenda` open every one of them. The system modules sat in their own `env/` directory.\n\n**After:**\n- A new first module, `sp-paths`, names each location once (`sp-notes-dir`, `sp-documents-dir`, `sp-literature-dir`, `sp-bibliography-dir`, `sp-org-dir`, `sp-src-dir`, `sp-git-dir`, `sp-clones-dir`, `sp-data-home`, `sp-yadm-repo`, `sp-chrome-history-file`) and offers `sp-path` to build a path below one. The modules use these instead of literals. Each location can be overridden from the environment (`SP_NOTES_DIR`, `SP_BIBLIOGRAPHY_DIR`, `SP_DOCUMENTS_DIR`, `SP_ORG_DIR`, `SP_SRC_DIR`, `SP_GIT_DIR`, `SP_CLONES_DIR`, `XDG_DATA_HOME`). Defaults come from `~`, and the Chrome history path has a macOS, Windows and Linux default. This prepares for `sp-syswin` and the Linux module, which are not part of this PR.\n- `env/` moves to `base/` (`sp-env`, `sp-exwm`, `sp-macos`, `sp-syslinux`, `sp-syswin`), in `libraries/modules/` and in `docs/tangles/`. The tangle paths, `docs/main.org` and `conditional-loading.org` follow. `sp-env` requires `sp-paths` and explains in its commentary that the `SP_*` overrides are read before the shell environment is imported.\n- The whole Custom block at the end of `init.el` (`custom-set-variables` and `custom-set-faces`) is removed, so `sp-vulpea-para` decides which agenda files load. A copy of the removed block is kept outside the repo in case anything in it should come back.\n\n**Behaviour notes:**\n- On your Mac every path default resolves to what it was before.\n- Removing the Custom block also drops what it set besides the agenda files: `sp-ui-default-font` (PT Mono 120), `sp-ui-variable-width-font` (Aporetic Serif Mono 120), `sia/modeline` (doom-modeline), `custom-safe-themes`, `package-selected-packages`, `package-vc-selected-packages` (lambda-themes), `helm-minibuffer-history-key`, `transient-show-menu`, `bibtex-aux-opt-alist` and the four `org-extra-emphasis` faces. Fonts, the modeline and the emphasis colours will fall back to defaults until they are set in a module. Without a `custom-file`, Customize writes a new block into `init.el` again.\n- Left alone on purpose: `~/.config/...`, the legacy `~/.emacs.d` entries, `~/bin/mark.sh`, `~/opt/plantuml`, `~/.worktrees/` and plain `~/` starting directories.\n\n**How:** the literate sources in `docs/tangles/` are edited together with the modules. In Emacs 29.3 batch, `sp-paths.org` tangles to `sp-paths.el` identically, and the moved docs tangle to their modules unchanged. `sp-paths` is added at the top of the Core section of both module lists in `init.el` and of the profiles in `sp-config-profiles.el`. I loaded `sp-paths` with and without `SP_NOTES_DIR` and checked that every changed file reads. I did not start the full configuration, so please try a launch on your Mac.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015QV8A7ivyRigBtBymbF9FR\n",
